State the pressed scroll bar thumb as the hovered thumb

Style::drawSbSliderHandle() folds the pressed state and the on
state of a thumb into the hover state before any colour pick.
The widget rules stated no slider:active row, so an engine that
drops the prelight on a grab paints a dragged thumb with the
rest colour. The style then clears the two states, so the
hover pick stands alone.

Writer::scrollBar() now puts the hover box under the
slider:active selector as well. The rule reuses the hover
values, so the sheets declare no new custom property.

The shade tables and the path tables gain the rows of the new
rule. assert-scrollbar.sh binds the pressed row to the hover
row over every arm, with a control of its own.

The change sits on the branch work/gtk4-theme of the local tree, as the
sixteenth commit. The fork wyn/qtcurve holds that branch. Merge request !15
on system/qtcurve holds that branch.

Drop this patch when upstream merges the change.

